@@ -29,9 +29,11 @@ The consensus request carries the exact governed candidate count. Reviewing only
 
 A technically coherent review set is not enough. Before candidate-set consensus can enter the Docs Suite quality gate, `compileBookArtCandidateSetProviderRunReceipt` rebuilds one read-only receipt from the exact durable runtime job, verified candidate descriptors, verified candidate bytes and the provider evidence JSON.
 
-The receipt binds the candidate-set and work-order fingerprints to the runtime job ID and spec hash, the normalized provider request, compiled prompt, one successful adapter/model attempt, the evidence artifact and the ordered output set. Every reviewed candidate ID, content hash, descriptor fingerprint and producer must match that receipt through `evaluateBookArtCandidateSetExecutionConsensus`.
+The receipt binds the candidate-set and work-order fingerprints to the runtime job ID and spec hash, the normalized provider request, compiled prompt, one successful adapter/model attempt, the evidence artifact and the ordered output set. Every reviewed candidate ID, content hash, descriptor fingerprint and producer must match that receipt.
 
-Missing outputs, substituted bytes, reordered evidence, a different adapter, a fallback attempt, a redriven job, an altered request, an unverified artifact or a recomputed standalone review fingerprint all fail closed. The receipt compiler performs no provider call and writes no artifacts.
+`evaluateBookArtCandidateSetExecutionConsensus` does not trust a caller-supplied receipt. It accepts the exact provider job plan plus the consensus input, re-reads the durable runtime job and immutable artifacts, rebuilds the receipt internally, and only then evaluates the review set. A caller cannot turn changed runtime identity or output evidence into authority by recomputing a receipt fingerprint and updating the consensus digest.
+
+Missing outputs, substituted bytes, reordered evidence, a different adapter, a fallback attempt, a redriven job, an altered request, an unverified artifact, a recomputed standalone review fingerprint or a re-fingerprinted provider-run receipt all fail closed. Receipt compilation and execution-bound evaluation perform no provider call and write no artifacts.
